{"records":[{"id":"sgyzkr223j","title":"Single live cell monitoring of protein turnover reveals intercellular variability and cell cycle dependence of degradation rates, Alber et al","description":"Time lapse datasets of tandem-fluorescent timer-tagged endogenous proteins in mouse embryonic stem cells, and SNAP-tagged and Halo-tagged proteins in mouse embryonic stem cells.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-07-26T06:28:05.441Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sgyzkr223j","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sgyzkr223j"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Suter","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Mathematical Modeling","Stem Cell","Protein Synthesis","Protein Degradation","Fluorescent Labels"],"journal_issn":["10972765"]},{"id":"z48dr3bx9z","title":"Uncropped immunoblots in \"Peroxisome-dependent and -independent functions of PEX19 in mouse embryonic stem cells\"","description":"Uncropped immunoblots in manuscript titled \"Peroxisome-dependent and -independent functions of PEX19 in mouse embryonic stem cells\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-11T06:51:43.857Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/z48dr3bx9z","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/z48dr3bx9z"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xiaoling","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/00j4k1h63","name":"National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences","grant_id":"Z01 ES102205"}],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b3ffg5k7hp","title":"Table S1 (TableS1.csv), related to step 15, Cosson et al","description":"This table contains the raw data from our mass spectrometry analysis for differential analysis of Trim71-associated protein complexes in mouse embryonic stem cells, including the sum of peptide peak intensities (beginning with 'Sumintensity'), numerical data in other columns, and additional information presented in text format. This file serves as support for the protocol published in Cosson B. et al., STAR Protocols, 2024, Protocol for differential analysis of Trim71-associated protein complexes in mouse embryonic stem cells by mass spectrometry using Perseus.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-05-22T17:51:43.008Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b3ffg5k7hp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b3ffg5k7hp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Bertrand","last_name":"Cosson","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Mass Spectrometry"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"m66wgvw7sm","title":"RNA polymerase II transcription initiation in holo-TFIID-depleted mouse embryonic stem cells","description":"Raw data for Western blots and cell counting associated to the following manuscript\n\nVincent Hisler, Paul Bardot, Dylane Detilleux, Andrea Bernardini, Matthieu Stierle, Emmanuel Garcia Sanchez, Claire Richard, Lynda Hadj Arab, Cynthia Ehrhard, Bastien Morlet, Yavor Hadzhiev, Matthieu Jung, Stéphanie Le Gras, Luc Négroni, Ferenc Müller, László Tora and Stéphane D. Vincent\nRNA polymerase II transcription initiation in holo-TFIID-depleted mouse embryonic stem cells\n\nIn these study, we analyzed the impact of the conditional deletion of two genes coding for tow distinct TFIID subunits TAF7 and TAF10 in mouse embryonic stem cells. We investigated the impact of these deletions on TFIID assembly, TFIID chromatin binding and nascent transcription to evaluate the ability of partial TFIID complex to initiate RNA polymerase II transcription initiation.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-09-12T09:53:06.197Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/m66wgvw7sm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/m66wgvw7sm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"STEPHANE","last_name":"VINCENT","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Transcription","Mouse","Embryonic Stem Cell"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"v4v9wgthwg","title":"Inter-chromosomal contact properties in live-cell imaging and in Hi-C","description":"- unprocessed z-stacks of CLING images as single tif files\n- spatial distances between two given loci (measured in micrometer)\n- speed measurements of 4D-CLING (time-lapse imaging)\n- Hi-C matrices of mouse embryonic stem cells and human RPE-1 cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-03-22T23:54:03.395Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/v4v9wgthwg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/v4v9wgthwg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Philipp","last_name":"Maass","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Natural Sciences"],"journal_issn":["10972765"]},{"id":"nb9hh8yyds","title":"Cross-regulation between TDP-43 and paraspeckles promotes pluripotency-differentiation transition","description":"additional supplementary data:\n- Sanger sequencing and confirmatory gel electrophoresis confirming the CRISPR-Cas9 edited human and mouse embryonic stem cells presented in the manuscript under review.\n\n- additional supplementary data: raw unprocessed confocal images presented in Fig2 of the manuscript under review: ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-03-18T19:45:41.433Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nb9hh8yyds","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nb9hh8yyds"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Miha","last_name":"Modic","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jernej","last_name":"Ule","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Micha","last_name":"Drukker","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing","Western Blot","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hbr8p7n526","title":"Cross-regulation between TDP-43 and paraspeckles promotes pluripotency-differentiation transition. Modic et al","description":"Sanger sequencing and confirmatory gel electrophoresis confirming the CRISPR-Cas9 edited human and mouse embryonic stem cells presented in the manuscript under review entitled \"Cross-regulation between TDP-43 and paraspeckles promotes pluripotency-differentiation transition\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-03-19T17:58:48.63Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hbr8p7n526","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hbr8p7n526"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"micha","last_name":"drukker","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7ny8bnz73y","title":"SPT6 Regulates H3K14Ac Deposition in Mouse Embryonic Stem Cells","description":"WB of Figures 1A, 4A, 4B, 4C, S2B, S2C, S4B, S4E, S4F, S6E.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-02-26T15:56:17.777Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7ny8bnz73y","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7ny8bnz73y"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Hongjie","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Life Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"sb72467mrf","title":"Mouse glutamatergic neurons immunofluorescence images upon Suz12 isoforms deletions","description":"The Polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) mediates epigenetic maintenance of gene silencing in eukaryotes via methylation of histone H3 at lysine 27 (H3K27). \nAlternative splicing (AS) of the PRC2 core component SUZ12 generates an uncharacterised isoform SUZ12-S, which co-exists with the canonical SUZ12-L isoform in the same cell in virtually all tissues and developmental stages. While SUZ12-S is necessary and sufficient to ensure correct repression of Polycomb target genes via promoter-proximal H3K27me3 deposition, SUZ12-L is needed for maintaining global H3K27 methylation levels. We showed that mouse embryonic stem cells (ESCs) lacking either of the two isoforms have a slower exit from pluripotency and fail to acquire neuronal cell identity upon differentiation stimuli. This dataset contains raw immunofluorescence images of ESCs derived neurons stained for H3K27me3 (RRID:AB_2614987), MAP2 (RRID:AB_2138153), and TUBB3 (RRID:AB_2564645). All images were counter-stained with DAPI before mounting. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-01-25T06:37:16.184Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sb72467mrf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sb72467mrf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Niccolò","last_name":"Arecco","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wx6s4mj7s8","title":"Nanog STILT inference","description":"1) Distributions of the sampled trajectories using STILT on the Nanog subtree dataset\n2) Goodness-of-fit test distributions\n\nRelated to : \nAnalysis of cell lineage trees by exact Bayesian inference identifies negative autoregulation of Nanog in mouse embryonic stem cells.\n\nFeigelman, et al. Cell Systems. 2016.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-10-28T16:09:18.292Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wx6s4mj7s8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wx6s4mj7s8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Justin","last_name":"Feigelman","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Statistics"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":139769,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":138,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":139769,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":139036,"restricted":69,"embargoed":664},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd9